THIS IS THE MUNALE OF THE CODE , WHAT IT DOES AND THE LIBRARIS USED IN IT 

It simulates health monitoring for an 8-thruster system by generating random values for voltage, temperature, CPU
All you need is one to do it to run the code
It keeps checking the health when random numbers are added and if any error occurs of the health it pauses all the 8-thrusters for 5 seconds
 I used import time for timing delays
 import random to add random numbers for the voltage, temperature, CPU
import os alongside import sys for platform detection and to exit the project completely and safely
 To enable non-blocking keyboard input across operating systems and  to know what key was pressed
i used key detection using import msvcrt on Windows and import select, import termios, import tty on macOS or Linux
 allowing the simulation to run until the user presses 'q' to quit

I used Gemini to help me in many concepts and in understanding them.
